#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bus-nudge delivery adapter -- codex. THE CONTRACT, UNIMPLEMENTED.

This file exists so that the shape of the work is written down and so that a
machine which selects this substrate is refused out loud rather than nudging
nobody in silence. It delivers nothing and it never will until somebody writes
the three answers below.

THE ADAPTER CONTRACT, WHICH EVERY ADAPTER HERE ANSWERS AND NONE MAY WIDEN:

  1. Deliver the fixed text, verbatim, to a live consenting session.
  2. Refuse the dead without resurrecting them.
  3. Fail loudly when the transport changes.

  adapter probe     {} on stdin -> {"substrate","present","reason"}
  adapter deliver   the target on stdin -> {"outcome","reason","detail"}
                    outcome is delivered | refused | failed
                    exit 0 for delivered and refused, 3 for failed

WHAT WRITING THIS ADAPTER REQUIRES. Three questions, and none of them has an
answer that can be assumed from another substrate:

  1. WHAT IS THE TRANSPORT? Name the thing an outside process writes to so that
     a running session reads a line: a socket, a fifo, a CLI verb, a pane. Then
     name what proves it arrived, because a write that reports success into a
     void is worse than one that fails.
  2. WHAT IS CONSENT, AND WHERE IS IT WRITTEN? Every substrate has one. On
     Claude sessions it is a settings value the recipient sets; on tmux it is
     the act of registering a pane. Find the equivalent, read it, and refuse
     when it is absent. Never forge it, and never widen the gate from outside.
  3. HOW IS A DEAD SESSION TOLD FROM A LIVE ONE, WITHOUT REVIVING IT? A record
     that a session existed is not a session. Where the only way to reach a
     recorded session is to restart it, the answer is refusal: a restart makes
     a second copy of a unit and leaves the first one dead.

The payload the core sends carries: handle, bus_dir, session, pid, owner,
address, pane, cwd, unread, text. Deliver `text` and nothing else -- this file
must never compose a sentence.
"""

import json
import sys

REASON = ("the codex adapter is a documented stub: no transport, no consent rule and "
          "no liveness test has been written for this substrate, so nothing can be "
          "delivered on it")


def main():
    verb = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else ""
    if verb == "probe":
        print(json.dumps({"substrate": "codex", "present": False, "reason": REASON}))
        return 0
    if verb == "deliver":
        print(json.dumps({"outcome": "failed", "reason": "no adapter for this substrate",
                          "detail": REASON}))
        return 3
    sys.stderr.write(__doc__)
    return 2


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
